<title>JAPAN: General Sekiyu refinery to close in May for checks.</title>
<headline>General Sekiyu refinery to close in May for checks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Sekiyu KK said on Wednesday it would close its Sakai refinery for routine maintenance checks in mid-May.</p>
<p>General Sekiyu's turnaround schedule is as follows:</p>
<p>Facility		   Capacity			  Date</p>
<p>			 (barrels per day)</p>
<p>Crude distillation</p>
<p>  unit		     156,000		36 days from May 14</p>
<p>Vacuum distillation     70,000		36 days from May 16</p>
<p>Catalytic cracker	 40,000		May 14 - June 18</p>
<p>Catalytic reformer	34,000		May 14 - June 18</p>
<p>Naphtha desulphuriser   40,000		May 14 - June 18</p>
<p>Kerosene/gas oil</p>
<p>  desulphuriser	   76,400		May 14 - June 18</p>
<p>Indirect desulphuriser  40,000		May 16 - June 20</p>
<p>General Sekiyu KK is owned 49 percent by Exxon Corp.</p>
</text>
